---
// src/pages/vmware-alternatives.astro
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout 
  title="VMware Alternatives & Hypervisor Migration | InfraHub"
  description="Evaluate enterprise VMware alternatives including Vates XCP-ng and Xen Orchestra, Proxmox VE, and other KVM or Xen-based approaches."
  canonicalPath="/vmware-alternatives"
>
  <div class="section section-hero network-overlay">
    <div class="container service-container">
      <div class="service-header">
        <div class="header-badge-row">
          <span class="pill-badge badge-blue">Virtualization</span>
          <span class="pill-badge badge-teal">Partner Delivered</span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="service-title">Enterprise VMware Alternatives</h1>
        <p class="service-lead">
          VMware licensing, platform strategy, and operating-model changes have led many infrastructure teams to reassess their virtualization stack. InfraHub helps compare migration paths, operational trade-offs, support models, storage design, backup, and hardware requirements before selecting an alternative.
        </p>
        <div class="service-hero-actions">
          <a href="/partners/vates" class="btn btn-accent btn-lg">Explore Vates</a>
          <a href="/lets-talk?service=vmware-alternatives" class="btn btn-secondary btn-lg">Request Migration Assessment</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="content-section">
        <span class="section-sub-tag">Hypervisor Comparison</span>
        <h2>Virtualization Approaches to Evaluate</h2>
        <div class="problem-grid">
          <div class="problem-card">
            <h3>Vates VMS</h3>
            <p>Vates combines the open-source XCP-ng virtualization platform with Xen Orchestra for browser-based administration, VM-level backup, replication, metrics, and automation, backed by commercial Vates support and migration services.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="problem-card">
            <h3>Proxmox VE</h3>
            <p>A Debian-based virtualization environment built around KVM and containers, commonly evaluated for integrated clustering, storage, backup, and virtualization management.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="problem-card">
            <h3>Enterprise Linux KVM</h3>
            <p>A KVM-based approach can fit teams that prefer Linux-native virtualization building blocks and are prepared to assemble management, storage, backup, and automation around their operating model.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="content-section partner-context-section">
        <span class="section-sub-tag">Partner Context</span>
        <h2>Vates: XCP-ng & Xen Orchestra</h2>
        <p>
          Vates describes XCP-ng as its Xen-based open-source virtualization platform and Xen Orchestra as the web-based management, administration, and native VM-backup layer for XCP-ng. Vates also offers commercial support, consulting, and migration services around the stack.
        </p>
        <a href="/partners/vates" class="partner-context-link">View Vates partner profile →</a>
      </div>

      <div class="service-footer-cta">
        <h2>Plan the Migration Around the Workload</h2>
        <p>Start with cluster scale, storage, networking, backup, HA/DR, support expectations, and the downtime or migration constraints that matter to your applications.</p>
        <a href="/lets-talk?service=vmware-alternatives" class="btn btn-accent btn-lg">Discuss Your Virtualization Strategy</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .service-container { max-width: 1040px; }
  .service-header { text-align: left; max-width: 860px; margin: 0 0 64px; padding-bottom: 24px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-color); }
  .header-badge-row { display: flex; justify-content: flex-start; gap: 8px; margin-bottom: 16px; }
  .service-title { font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 4vw, 3.4rem); font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.15; margin-bottom: 20px; }
  .service-lead { font-size: 1.15rem; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.65; margin-bottom: 32px; }
  .service-hero-actions { display: flex; justify-content: flex-start; gap: 14px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .content-section { margin-bottom: 72px; }
  .section-sub-tag { display: block; font-family: var(--font-heading); font-size: 0.8rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.08em; color: var(--accent-blue); margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .content-section h2 { font-size: 1.85rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 18px; }
  .content-section > p { font-size: 1rem; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.65; max-width: 780px; }
  .problem-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 20px; }
  @media (min-width: 768px) { .problem-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); } }
  .problem-card { background-color: var(--bg-secondary); border: 1px solid var(--border-color); border-radius: var(--radius-lg); padding: 24px; }
  .problem-card h3 { font-size: 1.1rem; margin-bottom: 10px; color: var(--text-primary); }
  .problem-card p { font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.5; }
  .partner-context-section { border-top: 1px solid var(--border-color); padding-top: 40px; }
  .partner-context-link { display: inline-flex; margin-top: 18px; font-size: 0.92rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--accent-blue); }
  .partner-context-link:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  .service-footer-cta { padding: 40px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-start; text-align: left; gap: 16px; border-top: 1px solid var(--border-color); }
  .service-footer-cta p { color: var(--text-secondary); }
</style>
